    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "For individuals with moderate to severe depression, it can be difficult to manage decisions in everyday life. Research shows that depression reduces quality of life through cognitive distortions––biased perspectives that are considered irrational about oneself and the external world, creating damaging thought patterns and false beliefs. Such disparaging distortions make it especially important to be connected to supportive friends and family. Mindality is a platform that helps learners generate explanations of their day-to-day struggles. The goal is to enhance an individual’s capacity to effectively understand their own needs and communicate them to loved ones or licensed professionals in order to get support––and these self-generated explanations can leverage a variety of media, such as audio, text, and visual. The multimodal availability of expressing common symptoms found in depression and suicidal ideation proposes that this practice can potentially support mental health understanding, communication, and literacy for those impacted by mental health, both directly and indirectly. This report provides the reader with some research perspectives on major depressive disorder and its relationship to the effectiveness that multimedia can leverage for expression, communication, and support.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
